  "caveat": "Verify the concrete package pinout; unavailable pins are rejected by the core masks.",
  "data_quality_note": "The STC32F manual (2024-02-02), sections 1.4, 2.1 and 10.1, documents STC32F12K54 with 54 KiB program Flash at 0xFF0000-0xFFD7FF, 8 KiB EDATA and 4 KiB XDATA. The LQFP48 pin table exposes 44 GPIOs; P1.2 is absent and ADC channel 2 uses P5.4. The section 12 heading says 45 GPIOs but conflicts with the actual pin table; this variant follows the pin table. TFPU and its vendor ROM/library region are not exposed as Arduino APIs or user Flash. The 12 MHz experimental C++11 core uses a constrained 3584-byte heap and preserves 512 XDATA bytes for static state; exact-QEMU qualification is tracked separately. It is unrelated to ARM-based STC32F03x parts."
